01:45:36.590 --> 01:45:37.590
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

01:45:37.590 --> 01:45:38.590
Part of the fun of the Scream franchise and
the whodunit genre in general

01:45:38.590 --> 01:45:39.590
is going back to see the clues laid out for
us once we know the ending.

01:45:39.590 --> 01:45:40.590
In Tara's dialogue with Quinn at the apartment,
Quinn describes how her dad

01:45:40.590 --> 01:45:41.590
held on too tight with overprotectiveness
after they lost her brother.

01:45:41.590 --> 01:45:42.590
Combine that with Detective Bailey's line
after Quinn's death.

01:45:42.590 --> 01:45:43.590
-[Detective Bailey] Both my kids are gone,
my whole family is gone.

01:45:43.590 --> 01:45:46.199
And that's two oddly specific references to
this mysterious dead sibling.

01:45:46.199 --> 01:45:48.860
The movie honestly could have used a few red
herrings to throw us off

01:45:48.860 --> 01:45:50.781
because it was obvious that this brother was
significant.

01:45:50.781 --> 01:45:54.619
Add in the fact that the first Ghostface call
comes from Richie Kirsch's

01:45:54.619 --> 01:45:56.560
phone, and it starts to become clear.

01:45:56.560 --> 01:45:59.110
This is the same tactic that Richie and Amber
used.

01:45:59.110 --> 01:46:00.949
When a call came in from Amber's phone,

01:46:00.949 --> 01:46:03.199
everyone assumed that the killer cloned Amber's
phone number,

01:46:03.199 --> 01:46:06.929
when in reality, all they had to do was use
Amber's actual phone.

01:46:06.929 --> 01:46:09.739
Detective Bailey probably got Richie's phone
back after his death and just

01:46:09.739 --> 01:46:13.550
used that. One area where the movie did successfully
employ a red herring was

01:46:13.550 --> 01:46:14.719
in wardrobe.

01:46:14.719 --> 01:46:17.989
Fans know at this point that at least one
Ghostface killer always has a

01:46:17.989 --> 01:46:19.469
light blue shirt or flannel.

01:46:19.469 --> 01:46:20.949
In this case, it was Ethan,

01:46:20.949 --> 01:46:24.310
and while I never really suspected Tara or
Sam, we're forced to notice Danny

01:46:24.310 --> 01:46:27.270
wearing light blue when we literally see him
put it on.

01:46:27.270 --> 01:46:30.219
Someone wearing a Ghostface mask attacks Sam
and Tara outside their apartment,

01:46:30.219 --> 01:46:33.150
the same apartment where they were literally
just with Quinn and Ethan.

01:46:33.150 --> 01:46:35.969
Later on, after Quinn's death is staged, her
father comes out of the

01:46:35.969 --> 01:46:38.910
building with a little bit of a limp, maybe
from an injury sustained when

01:46:38.910 --> 01:46:40.840
he's knocked to the floor by Samantha.

01:46:40.840 --> 01:46:43.500
And he's staring right at Samantha as he says
this.

01:46:43.500 --> 01:46:48.190
-[Detective Bailey] You f*** with my family,
you die.

01:46:48.190 --> 01:46:50.360
And when Gale gets the dreaded phone call
later on.

01:46:50.360 --> 01:46:53.830
It's from a 707 area code, which represents
Northern California, where

01:46:53.830 --> 01:46:55.389
Woodsboro is located.

01:46:55.389 --> 01:46:58.280
That's another clue that the killer is from
that area, which Richie's family

01:46:58.280 --> 01:46:59.710
most likely would be.

01:46:59.710 --> 01:47:03.610
There's also an ominous clue that isn't related
to the identity of the protagonist.

01:47:03.610 --> 01:47:06.500
Sam's psychiatrist can be seen watching Invasion
of the Body Snatchers

01:47:06.500 --> 01:47:11.560
which literally tells him before he becomes
the next Ghostface victim.

01:47:11.560 --> 01:47:14.619
As always, it's one of many horror movie references
in a Scream film.

01:47:14.619 --> 01:47:17.270
Every Scream movie makes a reference to Psycho,
with the last film

01:47:17.270 --> 01:47:20.900
even containing a Psycho movie poster. That
continues here with this poster

01:47:20.900 --> 01:47:21.949
in Jason's apartment.

01:47:21.949 --> 01:47:25.610
He also has a Vertigo poster, another thriller
directed by Alfred Hitchcock.

01:47:25.610 --> 01:47:28.780
In addition to the first Psycho, Psycho Two
is also referenced this time.

01:47:28.780 --> 01:47:31.250
–[Mindy &amp; Kirby] Psycho II is underrated.

01:47:31.250 --> 01:47:34.120
Psycho Two also features a character getting
stabbed through the mouth,

01:47:34.120 --> 01:47:36.739
which is exactly what Tara does to Ethan at
the end.

01:47:36.739 --> 01:47:39.699
But going back to Jason, given that he's a
film student and a horror fan,

01:47:39.699 --> 01:47:41.739
there are a lot of references connected to
him.

01:47:41.739 --> 01:47:44.230
The reason he killed his professor in the
opening sequence was because she

01:47:44.230 --> 01:47:46.160
gave him a C-minus on his Giallo paper.

01:47:46.160 --> 01:47:50.239
Giallo is an Italian murder mystery genre,
a perfect counterpart to Scream.

01:47:50.239 --> 01:47:54.010
Jason's t-shirt says 4 Mosche On Velluto Grigio,
which translates to

01:47:54.010 --> 01:47:55.750
four flies on the gray velvet.

01:47:55.750 --> 01:47:59.000
It's a Giallo film directed by Dario Argento
about a rock musician who

01:47:59.000 --> 01:48:01.360
becomes entangled in a gruesome murder case.

01:48:01.360 --> 01:48:04.340
Interestingly, Jason also has an Ice Nine
Kills magnet on his fridge.

01:48:04.340 --> 01:48:07.720
Ice Nine Kills is a metal band known for theming
their songs around horror movies.

01:48:07.720 --> 01:48:10.760
Their 2018 album, The Silver Scream has a
series of accompanying

01:48:10.760 --> 01:48:13.780
music videos with a narrative through line
about a series of deaths connected

01:48:13.780 --> 01:48:15.930
to the band's frontman Spencer Charnas.

01:48:15.930 --> 01:48:19.340
So kind of similar to Four Flies on the Gray
Velvet. Ice Nine Kills also did

01:48:19.340 --> 01:48:22.780
a deluxe version of The Silver Scream, which
appropriately contains a song

01:48:22.780 --> 01:48:23.949
about Scream.

01:48:23.949 --> 01:48:26.909
And no, it was not lost on me that Jason gets
home and turns on a

01:48:26.909 --> 01:48:28.280
Friday the 13th movie.

01:48:28.280 --> 01:48:32.280
His full name is Jason Carvey, and Jason Voorhees,
the antagonist of the

01:48:32.280 --> 01:48:35.500
Friday the 13th franchise, likes to carve
up his victims.

01:48:35.500 --> 01:48:37.780
This isn't just any Friday the 13th movie,
though.

01:48:37.780 --> 01:48:40.890
It's Friday the 13th Part VIII: Jason Takes
Manhattan.

01:48:40.890 --> 01:48:42.400
The one where he goes to New York.

01:48:42.400 --> 01:48:44.989
Much like how Scream VI is set in New York.

01:48:44.989 --> 01:48:47.810
Jason is not the only new character who seems
to be a horror fan.

01:48:47.810 --> 01:48:50.239
Sam's psychiatrist has some merch in his office.

01:48:50.239 --> 01:48:53.780
On the desk, you can spot a lineup of horror
dolls, including Gomez, Pugsley

01:48:53.780 --> 01:48:55.560
and Fester Addams, as well as Leatherface.

01:48:55.560 --> 01:48:59.240
Above the fireplace, there's also a Leatherface
doll and a Ghostface doll.

01:48:59.240 --> 01:49:02.040
The defunct movie theater marquee is advertising
two events.

01:49:02.040 --> 01:49:04.599
On the left, it says Jennifer Jolie Retrospective.

01:49:04.599 --> 01:49:08.000
Jennifer Jolie was the name of the actress
who played Gale Weathers in Stab 3.

01:49:08.000 --> 01:49:11.179
On the right, it says Rocky Horror Picture
Show, which connects to

01:49:11.179 --> 01:49:15.060
this guy dressed up as Frank-n-Furter from
Rocky Horror on the subway.

01:49:15.060 --> 01:49:17.449
Which brings me to the next section the costumes.

01:49:17.449 --> 01:49:20.619
It's always been a pet peeve of mine in movies
that take place around

01:49:20.619 --> 01:49:23.610
Halloween, when everyone is dressed in generic
costumes like vampire,

01:49:23.610 --> 01:49:27.680
pirate, nurse, et cetera, because in real
life, most people are dressed up

01:49:27.680 --> 01:49:30.290
as something specific, usually some kind of
pop culture thing.

01:49:30.290 --> 01:49:32.520
I was glad to see Scream finally do this right

01:49:32.520 --> 01:49:36.460
and some of the costumes have a deeper meaning.
Like at the Omega Kappa Beta party,

01:49:36.460 --> 01:49:39.639
where we see a girl dressed as Wednesday Addams
from The Addams family.

01:49:39.639 --> 01:49:43.280
Since the release of Scream 2022, the star
Jenna Ortega portrayed this

01:49:43.280 --> 01:49:46.219
character in a popular adaptation known as
Wednesday.

01:49:46.219 --> 01:49:50.070
Is the recycling Wednesday flyer on her fridge
related to this as well?

01:49:50.070 --> 01:49:51.070
Probably not.

01:49:51.070 --> 01:49:54.010
Other party guests include someone in a striped
Ghostface mask hanging with

01:49:54.010 --> 01:49:55.340
Dwight Schrute from The Office.

01:49:55.340 --> 01:49:58.540
There's also a girl in the crowd wearing a
number ten jersey, a reference to

01:49:58.540 --> 01:50:01.690
the top that Tatum wears in the first Scream,
which is a reference to what

01:50:01.690 --> 01:50:04.110
Glen Lantz wore in A Nightmare on Elm Street.

01:50:04.110 --> 01:50:08.041
Then we've got Harry Potter, Alan from The
Hangover, and Mindy Meeks, who is

01:50:08.041 --> 01:50:11.440
dressed as Stormé DeLarverie, a woman known
for her part in a lesbian

01:50:11.440 --> 01:50:13.130
movement in the 1960s.

01:50:13.130 --> 01:50:15.179
That's kind of her whole entire gimmick in
this movie.

01:50:15.179 --> 01:50:17.210
She's constantly advertising her homosexuality.

01:50:17.210 --> 01:50:20.010
There are even more costumes in the subway
scene.

01:50:20.010 --> 01:50:23.869
First, there's Grace from the 2019 movie Ready
or Not, which is directed by

01:50:23.869 --> 01:50:26.389
Matt Bettinelli-Olpin and Tyler Gillett.

01:50:26.389 --> 01:50:29.500
Just like this movie, there's a David Bowie
in the crowd and a Michael Myers

01:50:29.500 --> 01:50:32.340
from the Halloween franchise, which is significant
because of how the Scream

01:50:32.340 --> 01:50:35.240
franchise is a satire primarily of the Halloween
franchise.

01:50:35.240 --> 01:50:39.340
In fact, when they arrive at the train station,
you can hear people chanting, Evil dies tonight.

01:50:39.340 --> 01:50:41.719
-[Jason] Less scary serial killer movie.

01:50:41.719 --> 01:50:44.730
Which is the mantra from Halloween, kills
the sequel to the requel.

01:50:44.730 --> 01:50:47.320
Just like how Scream VI is a sequel to a requel.

01:50:47.320 --> 01:50:49.240
The Statue of Liberty makes an appearance.

01:50:49.240 --> 01:50:50.240
Makes sense.

01:50:50.240 --> 01:50:51.240
It's New York.

01:50:51.240 --> 01:50:53.500
This is Mojo Jojo, the main villain from the
Powerpuff Girls.

01:50:53.500 --> 01:50:55.790
Nice to see Scream staying in touch with its
90s roots.

01:50:55.790 --> 01:50:58.850
It's not really a costume, but this guy has
a Fangoria shirt.

01:50:58.850 --> 01:51:01.020
Fangoria being the famous horror magazine.

01:51:01.020 --> 01:51:03.980
On the train, there's someone dressed as The
Babadook, which Tara cited as

01:51:03.980 --> 01:51:05.570
her favorite movie in the fifth Scream.

01:51:05.570 --> 01:51:10.040
-[Ghostface] What's your favorite scary movie?
-[Tara] The Babadook.

01:51:10.040 --> 01:51:13.429
Other than Ghostface, the train contains a
variety of other slasher icons,

01:51:13.429 --> 01:51:17.099
like Pinhead from the Hellraiser movies, Jason
from Friday the 13th, and

01:51:17.099 --> 01:51:18.900
Freddie Krueger from A Nightmare on Elm Street.

01:51:18.900 --> 01:51:22.050
Of course, this wasn't Freddie's first rodeo
in a Scream movie.

01:51:22.050 --> 01:51:24.599
There's also someone dressed as Chucky from
Child's Play, which was

01:51:24.599 --> 01:51:28.489
referenced in Scream 2022 as an example of
a horror movie that was remade.

01:51:28.489 --> 01:51:30.530
That scene also talks about elevated Horror.

01:51:30.530 --> 01:51:35.320
-[Amber]What's wrong with elevated horror?
I mean, Jordan Peele fucking rules.

01:51:35.320 --> 01:51:38.989
So some of the costumes in the subway are
from the elevated horror era, like

01:51:38.989 --> 01:51:42.040
Pluto from Jordan Peele's US, as well as several
of the other tethered

01:51:42.040 --> 01:51:43.480
characters from that movie.

01:51:43.480 --> 01:51:47.030
There's also a chick dressed as Dani Ardor,
aka The May Queen from Midsommar.

01:51:47.030 --> 01:51:49.969
Right after that, there's a quick flash cameo
from Tyler Gillett,

01:51:49.969 --> 01:51:53.230
the co-director, before we move on to some
Stephen King references.

01:51:53.230 --> 01:51:55.570
Including the Grady twins from The Shining
and Georgie Denbrough

01:51:55.570 --> 01:51:56.570
from IT.

01:51:56.570 --> 01:52:00.349
Other horror references include Melanie Daniels
from The Birds, complete with Bird,

01:52:00.349 --> 01:52:03.929
Horace Pinker from Wes Craven's Shocker, Kayako
Saeki from The Grudge,

01:52:03.929 --> 01:52:06.560
and Billy the Puppet from Saw, which was mentioned
in Scre4m.

01:52:06.560 --> 01:52:10.489
-[Trudie] Did you pick a movie?
-[Sherrie] Yeah, we're going to go scary,

01:52:10.489 --> 01:52:11.489
Saw 4.

01:52:11.489 --> 01:52:14.619
It seems there are also other pop culture
references on the train, like Tyler Durden

01:52:14.619 --> 01:52:18.250
from Fight Club, and I didn't know what this
was, so I tried Googling hand

01:52:18.250 --> 01:52:21.409
around a neck costume, and apparently this
was just an Oscars dress from

01:52:21.409 --> 01:52:24.700
Julia Fox, an actress from the movie Uncut
Gems.

01:52:24.700 --> 01:52:27.030
There's one glaring hole in the train scene.

01:52:27.030 --> 01:52:30.530
They're trying to safely travel from the Upper
West Side to the movie theater

01:52:30.530 --> 01:52:32.969
Everyone is in costume around them, so why
don't they just get

01:52:32.969 --> 01:52:36.800
costumes to evade Ghostface? There are many
hidden details in the costumes,

01:52:36.800 --> 01:52:39.739
and there may even be some that I didn't recognize,
so let me know what you

01:52:39.739 --> 01:52:40.739
saw in the comments.

01:52:40.739 --> 01:52:44.369
But there are even more secrets in the form
of hidden Wes Craven homages,

01:52:44.369 --> 01:52:49.260
Scream easter eggs, and other things you might
have missed.

01:52:49.260 --> 01:52:51.699
(Thunder)

01:52:51.699 --> 01:52:56.600
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

01:52:56.600 --> 01:52:57.639
If you follow my channel,

01:52:57.639 --> 01:53:00.500
you know I am very concerned with movie timeline
accuracy.

01:53:00.500 --> 01:53:03.869
I have a series called Horror History, which
is half character analysis and

01:53:03.869 --> 01:53:07.280
half timeline construction, so I can be the
first to say that these last two

01:53:07.280 --> 01:53:10.040
Scream movies have screwed up the timeline.

01:53:10.040 --> 01:53:12.369
At the end of the fifth Scream, the reporter
claims that the original

01:53:12.369 --> 01:53:15.389
Woodsboro Massacre was 25 years ago, almost
to the day.

01:53:15.389 --> 01:53:19.489
The original was set in 1996, so that would
mean that it was set in 2021.

01:53:19.489 --> 01:53:23.739
However, Sam and Mindy both claim that the
most recent Stab came out last year,

01:53:23.739 --> 01:53:27.460
and we can clearly see that was 2021, meaning
that the fifth Scream is

01:53:27.460 --> 01:53:31.530
actually set in 2022, which seems to be backed
up in Scream VI.

01:53:31.530 --> 01:53:34.239
The Woodsboro Truther subreddit refers to
the most recent events in

01:53:34.239 --> 01:53:37.820
Woodsboro as the 2022 Woodsboro Massacre,
and Kirby's timeline of

01:53:37.820 --> 01:53:41.429
events says 2022 was the year of Richie and
Amber's death.

01:53:41.429 --> 01:53:45.989
However, this board also claims that Roman's
death was in 2000, which is incorrect.

01:53:45.989 --> 01:53:48.699
In Scream 3, Roman died in 1999.

01:53:48.699 --> 01:53:51.480
The production designers obviously just use
the release dates of the movies

01:53:51.480 --> 01:53:55.340
rather than when they are set, but Kirby specifically
says that Richie and

01:53:55.340 --> 01:53:56.429
Amber died last year.

01:53:56.429 --> 01:53:59.770
So we can probably just go with the fifth
Scream taking place in 2022, and

01:53:59.770 --> 01:54:02.140
the sixth Scream taking place in 2023, right?

01:54:02.140 --> 01:54:05.400
Well, when we see the film professor's phone
at the beginning of the

01:54:05.400 --> 01:54:09.889
movie, it says Saturday, October 29, which
would put this in 2022.

01:54:09.889 --> 01:54:11.949
Other phone screens also corroborate this.

01:54:11.949 --> 01:54:15.500
Sam's driver's license is two days away from
expiration, although you could

01:54:15.500 --> 01:54:18.040
argue that she's not planning on renewing
it because you don't need a car in

01:54:18.040 --> 01:54:19.040
New York.

01:54:19.040 --> 01:54:22.159
And the subway map says service suspended
through September 2022.

01:54:22.159 --> 01:54:25.800
Why would that still be up over a year later?
But on the other hand, the

01:54:25.800 --> 01:54:28.820
newscaster in Scream VI very clearly refers
to Sam as...

01:54:28.820 --> 01:54:32.480
-[Reporter] One of the survivors of the Woodsboro
killings in 2022.

01:54:32.480 --> 01:54:36.679
So I think there's more evidence now that
Scream 2022 does in fact take

01:54:36.679 --> 01:54:41.810
place in 2022, and Scream VI takes place 13
months later in 2023.

01:54:41.810 --> 01:54:45.280
This board also confirms that the Scream TV
show is a separate canon

01:54:45.280 --> 01:54:47.570
entirely, which I'm very much fine with.

01:54:47.570 --> 01:54:50.290
Look, if anyone knows the people that work
on these movies, can you please

01:54:50.290 --> 01:54:53.590
just send them my channel so they can stop
screwing up their own franchise?

01:54:53.590 --> 01:54:56.659
I usually try to find a reason to make the
mistakes work by saying things

01:54:56.659 --> 01:54:59.790
like, this character was just estimating the
date, but there are only so

01:54:59.790 --> 01:55:01.489
many excuses I can make for you.

01:55:01.489 --> 01:55:03.530
-[Kirby] Roman Bridger was the only single
Ghostface.

01:55:03.530 --> 01:55:05.520
-[Kirby] Kudos to him for ambition.

01:55:05.520 --> 01:55:06.520
That's debatable.

01:55:06.520 --> 01:55:07.520
It's extremely debatable.

01:55:07.520 --> 01:55:10.489
See my Scream 3 Things You Missed episode
for details, but not until

01:55:10.489 --> 01:55:14.100
after you've seen all the Wes Craven references
here in Scream VI.

01:55:14.100 --> 01:55:17.010
As you know, Wes craven was the legendary
horror director who brought us

01:55:17.010 --> 01:55:20.280
everything from Last House on the Left, to
The Hills Have Eyes, to

01:55:20.280 --> 01:55:21.520
A Nightmare on Elm Street.

01:55:21.520 --> 01:55:24.239
And, of course, the first four Scream. In
Jason's apartment,

01:55:24.239 --> 01:55:27.409
he has up a poster for Last Podcast on the
Left, a clear play on

01:55:27.409 --> 01:55:28.739
Last House on the Left.

01:55:28.739 --> 01:55:32.159
That film was released in 1972, and in the
establishing shots at the

01:55:32.159 --> 01:55:34.849
beginning of the movie, we see West 72nd street.

01:55:34.849 --> 01:55:38.199
It appears that all of the east-west streets
in Upper Manhattan corresponds

01:55:38.199 --> 01:55:39.909
to Wes Craven release dates.

01:55:39.909 --> 01:55:43.159
The characters board a train at 94th and 93rd,
which corresponds to

01:55:43.159 --> 01:55:45.599
New Nightmare and Body Bags, respectively.

01:55:45.599 --> 01:55:48.590
Gale's apartment is located between 96th and
97th.

01:55:48.590 --> 01:55:51.380
Scream came out in 1996, and Scream 2 came
out in 1997.

01:55:51.380 --> 01:55:54.219
One of the posts in the Woodsboro Truther
subreddit,

01:55:54.219 --> 01:55:55.219
comes from a user named

01:55:55.219 --> 01:55:56.219
234Mimimimi23.

01:55:56.219 --> 01:55:59.949
Mimi Craven was Wes Craven's wife for a short
time

01:55:59.949 --> 01:56:00.949
in the 80s.

01:56:00.949 --> 01:56:03.449
She appeared in A Nightmare on Elm Street
and Swamp Thing.

01:56:03.449 --> 01:56:06.239
Jason and Greg's apartment building is called
Elmcourt, a reference to a

01:56:06.239 --> 01:56:08.760
Nightmare on Elm Street when we see Sam's
driver's license

01:56:08.760 --> 01:56:12.480
her address is 2419 Solar Drive, Modesto,
California.

01:56:12.480 --> 01:56:14.409
However, this address is not in Modesto.

01:56:14.409 --> 01:56:17.929
It's in Los Angeles, and it once belonged
to Wes Craven.

01:56:17.929 --> 01:56:19.659
This next one is one of the weirdest ever.

01:56:19.659 --> 01:56:22.610
At the end of the convenience store scene,
we see the exterior of the store,

01:56:22.610 --> 01:56:24.469
and it's called Abe's Snake Bodega.

01:56:24.469 --> 01:56:26.820
When I'm making these videos and I see a brand
name that I don't

01:56:26.820 --> 01:56:29.909
recognize, I always look it up to find out
if there's some significance.

01:56:29.909 --> 01:56:31.290
So that's what I did.

01:56:31.290 --> 01:56:34.239
And I found this Slashfilm article which contains
some odd trivia.

01:56:34.239 --> 01:56:37.070
It explains that one of Craven's friends got
involved in producing adult

01:56:37.070 --> 01:56:40.350
films in the 70's and he decided to try making
one himself.

01:56:40.350 --> 01:56:45.010
In 1975, in between the Last House and 1977s
the Hills Have Eyes, Craven made

01:56:45.010 --> 01:56:48.760
The Fireworks Woman, also known as Angela
the Fireworks Woman using a

01:56:48.760 --> 01:56:51.340
spectacular pseudonym Abe Snake.

01:56:51.340 --> 01:56:56.520
And just like Angela was packed with fireworks,
Scream VI is packed with

01:56:56.520 --> 01:56:59.079
Easter eggs, referencing the rest of the Scream
franchise.

01:56:59.079 --> 01:57:01.969
If you look closely at the Woodsboro truther
subreddit, which, by the

01:57:01.969 --> 01:57:05.520
way, the URL is www.r/woodsborotruther

01:57:05.520 --> 01:57:08.540
Pretty sure that's not how URLs work, but
you'll notice

01:57:08.540 --> 01:57:11.560
that the sub was created 1/14/2022.

01:57:11.560 --> 01:57:15.020
This contradicts the timeline again, but at
least this one is obviously just

01:57:15.020 --> 01:57:16.020
an Easter egg.

01:57:16.020 --> 01:57:19.869
It's technically the theatrical release date
of Scream 2022, seen on posters.

01:57:19.869 --> 01:57:21.600
Even though the premiere was canceled.

01:57:21.600 --> 01:57:23.320
Another Reddit post advertises.

01:57:23.320 --> 01:57:24.869
261 Turner Lane Part II.

01:57:24.869 --> 01:57:27.300
The All New True Story this is essentially
a story

01:57:27.300 --> 01:57:30.429
about the last movie's events because 261
Turner Lane is the

01:57:30.429 --> 01:57:33.869
address of the house once occupied by Stu
Macher and his family, before being

01:57:33.869 --> 01:57:35.520
the host of Amber Freeman and her family.

01:57:35.520 --> 01:57:38.119
-[Amber] I'm at Stu Macher's house on Turner
Lane.

01:57:38.119 --> 01:57:39.119
-[Amber] It's 261

01:57:39.119 --> 01:57:40.119
-[Amber] Turner Lane.

01:57:40.119 --> 01:57:42.160
Despite leaving Woodsboro, some of the characters
still seem to have

01:57:42.160 --> 01:57:43.659
pride about their old town.

01:57:43.659 --> 01:57:46.920
Chad hangs onto his letterman jacket and Mindy
wears a panther patch on

01:57:46.920 --> 01:57:48.950
hers, the mascot of Woodsboro High.

01:57:48.950 --> 01:57:52.480
One of the defining characteristics of a requel
is rehashing existing

01:57:52.480 --> 01:57:54.570
scenes, and Scream VI is no exception.

01:57:54.570 --> 01:57:57.380
Sam and Tara visit the police station following
their convenience store

01:57:57.380 --> 01:58:00.469
encounter, where they're told that they can't
leave town by the detectives.

01:58:00.469 --> 01:58:03.820
In the fourth Scream, Dewey and Judy have
to tell Sidney the same thing.

01:58:03.820 --> 01:58:06.570
Another Sidney parallel can be seen as they're
leaving and the media swarm

01:58:06.570 --> 01:58:10.219
around them, just like when they mobbed Sidney
Prescott in 1996 outside of

01:58:10.219 --> 01:58:11.610
the Woodsboro police station.

01:58:11.610 --> 01:58:13.440
And the same music plays as well.

01:58:13.440 --> 01:58:16.969
Eventually, Kirby shows up, now a member of
the FBI, and she and Mindy test

01:58:16.969 --> 01:58:18.679
each other on horror movie knowledge.

01:58:18.679 --> 01:58:21.949
– [Kirby] Best Nightmare on Elm Street?
– [Both] The original.

01:58:21.949 --> 01:58:25.150
This is a reference to the original Scream,
where Casey Becker has similar taste.

01:58:25.150 --> 01:58:26.150
-[Casey] Yeah, Freddie Krueger.

01:58:26.150 --> 01:58:27.150
-[Ghostface] Freddie. That's right.

01:58:27.150 --> 01:58:28.150
-[Ghostface] I like that movie.

01:58:28.150 --> 01:58:29.790
-[Ghostface] It was scary.

01:58:29.790 --> 01:58:33.730
-[Casey] Wow. The first one was, but the rest
sucks.

01:58:33.730 --> 01:58:35.409
Or maybe just common sense.

01:58:35.409 --> 01:58:36.409
Then there's Gale.

01:58:36.409 --> 01:58:39.270
During the part where she's talking with Sam
about the importance of family,

01:58:39.270 --> 01:58:42.350
we hear Dewey's theme in the background, suggesting
that Gale never stopped

01:58:42.350 --> 01:58:43.500
caring about him.

01:58:43.500 --> 01:58:46.579
This is also evident because she has the same
photo of her and Dewey that we

01:58:46.579 --> 01:58:48.910
first saw in Dewey's trailer in the fifth
one.

01:58:48.910 --> 01:58:51.869
She almost ended up joining him after an ambush
by Quinn.

01:58:51.869 --> 01:58:54.510
At one point, she fires two shots through
the door and says

01:58:54.510 --> 01:58:57.630
-[Gale] How's that for nostalgia, ******?

01:58:57.630 --> 01:59:01.160
Referring to when she played hero by shooting
Billy Loomis way back in the original.

01:59:01.160 --> 01:59:03.691
But it wasn't just the dialogue that was nostalgic,
because the movie

01:59:03.691 --> 01:59:06.980
theater shrine is packed with background detail
spanning the entire

01:59:06.980 --> 01:59:09.640
franchise.

01:59:09.640 --> 01:59:12.289
(Thunder)

01:59:12.289 --> 01:59:17.610
♪ Synth Music ♪

01:59:17.610 --> 01:59:20.650
Before heading into the theater for the final
showdown, Sam splits off from

01:59:20.650 --> 01:59:23.040
her new love interest, Danny, for safety reasons.

01:59:23.040 --> 01:59:27.130
-[Sam] We don't know you? Not really.

01:59:27.130 --> 01:59:30.800
She says this in almost the exact same way
as her old love interest.

01:59:30.800 --> 01:59:32.369
Richie, spoke about the Stab franchise.

01:59:32.369 --> 01:59:36.430
-[Richie] No one has made a great Stab movie
since the first one.

01:59:36.430 --> 01:59:37.760
-[Richie] Not really.

01:59:37.760 --> 01:59:39.810
From this point on, there's a lot of familiar
line delivery.

01:59:39.810 --> 01:59:40.810
-[Ethan] I've always wanted to stick something
in you, Tara.

01:59:40.810 --> 01:59:44.020
–[Stu] I always had a thing for you Sid!

01:59:44.020 --> 01:59:47.949
The movie theater shrine is a gold mine for
Things You Missed, akin to

01:59:47.949 --> 01:59:49.460
Eleanor's studio from Jigsaw.

01:59:49.460 --> 01:59:51.660
I'll start with the first Scream and work
my way forward.

01:59:51.660 --> 01:59:54.800
This is the outfit Tatum Riley wore on her
final night.

01:59:54.800 --> 01:59:57.350
This is Stu Macher's robe from the night of
his party.

01:59:57.350 --> 01:59:59.670
And here's Billy Loomis's shirt from that
same evening.

01:59:59.670 --> 02:00:02.360
The black jacket and backwards hat belong
to Kenny,

02:00:02.360 --> 02:00:04.610
Gale's Cameraman for Top Story with Gale Weathers.

02:00:04.610 --> 02:00:07.550
It's more obvious when you see the back of
his Top Story jacket.

02:00:07.550 --> 02:00:10.889
This mannequin represents Stephen Orth, Casey's
boyfriend and the franchise's

02:00:10.889 --> 02:00:12.570
first onscreen Kill.

02:00:12.570 --> 02:00:15.520
Here we have the Ghostface mask that Principal
Henry confiscated from the

02:00:15.520 --> 02:00:17.130
pranksters at the school and cut up.

02:00:17.130 --> 02:00:18.910
And these are the scissors he used to do it.

02:00:18.910 --> 02:00:22.140
-[Principal Henry] Two of your fellow students
just savagely murdered,

02:00:22.140 --> 02:00:26.969
-[Principal Henry] and this is the way that
you show your compassion and sensitivity.

02:00:26.969 --> 02:00:29.010
-[Principal Henry] Let me show you something.

02:00:29.010 --> 02:00:30.010
-[Principal Henry] You're both expelled. Get
out.

02:00:30.010 --> 02:00:31.679
You know, I wonder if they just showed up
at school the next day.

02:00:31.679 --> 02:00:34.560
It's not like Henry had time to tell anyone
that he expelled them.

02:00:34.560 --> 02:00:38.030
On top of the mask is the rope that Henry
swung from next to a sketch of

02:00:38.030 --> 02:00:40.750
where he was found on the football fields
and his obituaries.

02:00:40.750 --> 02:00:43.830
This is an employee shirt from Bradley Video
Store, the store that Randy

02:00:43.830 --> 02:00:45.199
worked at in the first movie.

02:00:45.199 --> 02:00:48.699
I'm not positive why this is here, because
as far as we know, nobody died at

02:00:48.699 --> 02:00:49.699
the video store.

02:00:49.699 --> 02:00:52.260
But I guess it's possible that it was still
a scene in the movie adaptation

02:00:52.260 --> 02:00:53.260
of Stab.

02:00:53.260 --> 02:00:56.340
Rounding out the first movie, we have the
Woodsboro High School Flag.

02:00:56.340 --> 02:00:58.929
Scream 2 opens with the Stab movie premiere,
and there's a lot of

02:00:58.929 --> 02:01:00.270
memorabilia from that.

02:01:00.270 --> 02:01:02.969
We see the costumes, masks and plastic knives
that were handed out to

02:01:02.969 --> 02:01:05.369
patrons in attendance at the premiere, as
well as a few

02:01:05.369 --> 02:01:06.369
movie tickets.

02:01:06.369 --> 02:01:09.159
In the corner is the giant Ghostface head
that decorated the production

02:01:09.159 --> 02:01:10.610
office in Scream 3.

02:01:10.610 --> 02:01:14.410
This sketch depicts Sidney at various points
in Scream 2 on stage, in the

02:01:14.410 --> 02:01:16.290
government car, and at the library.

02:01:16.290 --> 02:01:17.980
It's above a Windsor College sweater.

02:01:17.980 --> 02:01:21.199
The setting of Scream 2. I believe the camera
that Chad picks up and

02:01:21.199 --> 02:01:24.869
throws at Ghostface is Joel's camera during
his gig with Up to Date.

02:01:24.869 --> 02:01:27.909
This big old set piece along the side of the
theater is the thing that Derek

02:01:27.909 --> 02:01:29.790
was tied to at the end of Scream 2.

02:01:29.790 --> 02:01:32.840
And at some point, we can even see the Agamemnon
mask that he was wearing

02:01:32.840 --> 02:01:34.780
when he was lowered onto the stage.

02:01:34.780 --> 02:01:37.159
There's also another mask from that play right
here.

02:01:37.159 --> 02:01:40.780
There's also a glimpse of the white blazer
that Debbie Salt, Nancy Loomis,

02:01:40.780 --> 02:01:43.530
was wearing during the finale, and I believe
this is the gun that she used

02:01:43.530 --> 02:01:44.790
during that scene.

02:01:44.790 --> 02:01:47.389
Scream 3 is all about the production of the
third Stab movie being

02:01:47.389 --> 02:01:48.980
terrorized by a new threat.

02:01:48.980 --> 02:01:51.770
Above the Stab 3 script is the slate used
during filming.

02:01:51.770 --> 02:01:54.989
However, as an Easter egg, the cinematographer
is listed as Brett Jutkiewicz,

02:01:54.989 --> 02:01:58.100
the cinematographer of Scream 2022 and Scream
VI.

02:01:58.100 --> 02:02:01.659
I spotted a sketch of Sarah Darling, the first
Scream 3 victim, and

02:02:01.659 --> 02:02:03.980
Jennifer Jolie, the actress who played Gale.

02:02:03.980 --> 02:02:06.670
Also visible here is the killer's voice changer
and gun.

02:02:06.670 --> 02:02:09.320
Scream 3 had a special voice changer that
allowed the user to imitate

02:02:09.320 --> 02:02:10.410
anyone's voice.

02:02:10.410 --> 02:02:13.920
Kind of funny that we've only just recently
unlocked that technology today,

02:02:13.920 --> 02:02:17.219
and it's being used to make politicians bicker
over video games.

02:02:17.219 --> 02:02:20.670
In this case, there's a melted phone, a frying
pan and a lighter.

02:02:20.670 --> 02:02:23.239
The frying pan is the one that the killer
used to knock out the security

02:02:23.239 --> 02:02:24.500
guard, Stephen Stone.

02:02:24.500 --> 02:02:28.230
There's another frying pan attack in this
movie when Gale uses it against Quinn.

02:02:28.230 --> 02:02:30.079
I wonder if that one will make the next museum.

02:02:30.079 --> 02:02:33.550
The phone is Jennifer Jolie's phone, damaged
when her house exploded.

02:02:33.550 --> 02:02:36.220
And the lighter must have been Tom Prince's
lighter, which was responsible

02:02:36.220 --> 02:02:37.869
for causing that explosion.

02:02:37.869 --> 02:02:40.980
Overhead is the banner that says, Happy Birthday,
Roman, which was displayed

02:02:40.980 --> 02:02:43.989
over the entryway of John Milton's Manor when
Sidney arrived.

02:02:43.989 --> 02:02:47.070
It was not a happy birthday for Roman... Scre4m.

02:02:47.070 --> 02:02:50.329
By the time this one rolled around, several
more Stab films had been made.

02:02:50.329 --> 02:02:54.000
These posters for Stabs Three, Four and Five
are all in Scre4m, but this

02:02:54.000 --> 02:02:57.449
is the first time we've ever seen the Stab
Four poster, or should I say the

02:02:57.449 --> 02:02:59.750
St4b poster, unobstructed.

02:02:59.750 --> 02:03:02.951
There are also sketches of the two killers,
Charlie and Jill, as well as the

02:03:02.951 --> 02:03:06.140
shirt that Charlie was wearing when he died
and the flannel that Jill had on

02:03:06.140 --> 02:03:09.420
before being taken to the hospital and changed
into a hospital gown.

02:03:09.420 --> 02:03:12.179
There's a moment where we see Kirby looking
at it with tears in her eyes,

02:03:12.179 --> 02:03:15.980
remembering the way that her best friend betrayed
her and tried to have her killed.

02:03:15.980 --> 02:03:18.640
And we also see the knife that Charlie stabbed
her with and the

02:03:18.640 --> 02:03:21.190
residue on the patio where Kirby was tied
up.

02:03:21.190 --> 02:03:25.090
In the back, here you'll see the outfit worn
by Jill's ex-boyfriend, Trevor, when he died.

02:03:25.090 --> 02:03:28.880
It could also potentially be Neil Prescott's
outfit from Scream One, which

02:03:28.880 --> 02:03:29.880
looks the same.

02:03:29.880 --> 02:03:32.870
But since Neil never died, I'm guessing he
got to keep his clothes.

02:03:32.870 --> 02:03:35.720
I see no reason they would have ended up in
police custody.

02:03:35.720 --> 02:03:37.469
This one was the hardest to place.

02:03:37.469 --> 02:03:40.470
My first thought was that it was supposed
to be Casey Becker, because nobody

02:03:40.470 --> 02:03:42.390
else died in a white long sleeve.

02:03:42.390 --> 02:03:44.980
But it doesn't match, and she wasn't wearing
shorts.

02:03:44.980 --> 02:03:48.579
My guess is that it's actually supposed to
be Jill's neighbor, Olivia Morris,

02:03:48.579 --> 02:03:51.600
who was taken down while wearing a gray long
sleeve and flannel shorts.

02:03:51.600 --> 02:03:54.050
It's not a perfect match, but it's my best
guess.

02:03:54.050 --> 02:03:57.150
There's also a Woodsboro police uniform, meaning
that this belonged to

02:03:57.150 --> 02:04:00.739
Deputy Hoss or Deputy Perkins, the two cops
who fell in the line of duty

02:04:00.739 --> 02:04:02.949
while parked outside of Jill's house.

02:04:02.949 --> 02:04:04.989
And we have a Stabathon t-shirt.

02:04:04.989 --> 02:04:08.260
Stabathon was the movie marathon event hosted
by the Woodsboro High Film Club,

02:04:08.260 --> 02:04:10.270
where Gale Weathers was nearly butchered.

02:04:10.270 --> 02:04:13.480
In addition to those, there's also a case
full of Gale's books, most of

02:04:13.480 --> 02:04:27.130
which we've seen before in Scream 3 and Four,
with one notable addition.

02:04:27.130 --> 02:04:30.340
The Gale Weathers book that we haven't seen
before is Stabbed in the Back:

02:04:30.340 --> 02:04:31.780
The Real Sunrise Story.

02:04:31.780 --> 02:04:35.119
This actually comes from one of the promotional
websites for Scream 3,

02:04:35.119 --> 02:04:36.210
Sunrise Sucks.

02:04:36.210 --> 02:04:39.300
This was an anonymous expose site that published
dirt about the production

02:04:39.300 --> 02:04:41.880
company responsible for the Stab franchise,
Sunrise Studios.

02:04:41.880 --> 02:04:45.409
I talk about it extensively in my Horror History
episode on the history of

02:04:45.409 --> 02:04:46.409
the Stab IP.

02:04:46.409 --> 02:04:49.220
By the way, in Gale's apartment, there's one
new book called

02:04:49.220 --> 02:04:52.270
The Woodsboro Horror Continues, which must
be the one she wrote about the

02:04:52.270 --> 02:04:55.630
2022 or whenever it took place, Woodsboro
Massacre.

02:04:55.630 --> 02:04:59.260
All of these theater shrine items were part
of Richie Kirsch's collection,

02:04:59.260 --> 02:05:02.190
despite the fact that he claims that the first
Stab movie is the only good one.

02:05:02.190 --> 02:05:05.309
He dies in Scream 2022, so it makes sense
that there wouldn't be much

02:05:05.309 --> 02:05:06.320
from that movie.

02:05:06.320 --> 02:05:09.409
However, I did notice the Stab Blu-ray box-set,
which was released at some

02:05:09.409 --> 02:05:11.520
point between Screams Four and Five.

02:05:11.520 --> 02:05:14.380
If there's one thing you can usually count
on in a requel, it's the new

02:05:14.380 --> 02:05:16.829
characters taking up the mantle of the legacy
characters.

02:05:16.829 --> 02:05:20.000
In the case of Scream, Sam Carpenter is the
new Sidney Prescott, and she

02:05:20.000 --> 02:05:22.989
puts on the Ghostface costume to fight back
against Detective Bailey at the

02:05:22.989 --> 02:05:23.989
end of the movie.

02:05:23.989 --> 02:05:27.280
It's the very same Ghostface costume that
Sidney wore to strike back against

02:05:27.280 --> 02:05:30.280
Billy Loomis approximately 27 years earlier.

02:05:30.280 --> 02:05:33.700
And just like Billy, Bailey finds himself
on the wrong end of a Ghostface

02:05:33.700 --> 02:05:35.020
call from his prey.

02:05:35.020 --> 02:05:37.750
-[Sam] Hello, Detective Bailey.

02:05:37.750 --> 02:05:42.530
-[Sam] Are you alone in the house?

02:05:42.530 --> 02:05:47.580
Bailey is not the only one to suffer a very
1996 fate, Ethan pops up in the final reel

02:05:47.580 --> 02:05:51.950
for one last scare and gets crushed by the
same TV that fell upon Stu Macher.

02:05:51.950 --> 02:05:55.219
So what's the message this time? What are
the filmmakers trying to tell us?

02:05:55.219 --> 02:05:57.699
Well, it's not that different from the last
movie.

02:05:57.699 --> 02:06:00.719
This is kind of the second one in a row that
condemns toxic Internet

02:06:00.719 --> 02:06:03.829
culture. This time, instead of toxic fandom,
it's about the phenomenon of

02:06:03.829 --> 02:06:07.080
Reddit detectives who try to solve crimes
on their own and usually just end

02:06:07.080 --> 02:06:08.440
up making things worse.

02:06:08.440 --> 02:06:11.630
Wavywebsurf has a really good video on the
topic if you want to learn more.

02:06:11.630 --> 02:06:14.559
Throughout the movie, Sam has to deal with
accusations that she was actually

02:06:14.559 --> 02:06:17.800
the killer in Woodsboro, like this guy who
refers to her as being that

02:06:17.800 --> 02:06:18.800
psycho girl.

02:06:18.800 --> 02:06:20.530
He looks like he could be an actual Redditor.

02:06:20.530 --> 02:06:24.900
Another chick recognizes her, dumps diet Cherry
Coke on her, and calls her a murderer.

02:06:24.900 --> 02:06:27.350
Why would you dump a beverage on someone if
you believe she was a

02:06:27.350 --> 02:06:29.199
murderer? That is not a smart move.

02:06:29.199 --> 02:06:31.590
Even her psychiatrist starts to get creeped
out by her.

02:06:31.590 --> 02:06:34.309
If you're like me, you probably wanted to
go back and look at the names in

02:06:34.309 --> 02:06:36.980
the psychiatrist's filing cabinet to see if
there were any Easter eggs.

02:06:36.980 --> 02:06:40.969
As far as I can tell, these are just random
patient names with no deeper meaning.

02:06:40.969 --> 02:06:43.860
But Mars Jupiter is definitely a weird one.

02:06:43.860 --> 02:06:45.989
Perhaps the biggest twist with this movie
is that none of the core

02:06:45.989 --> 02:06:46.989
characters died.

02:06:46.989 --> 02:06:49.889
It looked like Chad was a goner there for
a minute, but he miraculously

02:06:49.889 --> 02:06:51.840
makes it out on a stretcher at the end.

02:06:51.840 --> 02:06:54.780
Although during that part where Tara takes
off his oxygen mask to kiss him,

02:06:54.780 --> 02:06:56.309
I wish he just would have died right there.

02:06:56.309 --> 02:06:59.260
It would have been so ******* funny.

02:06:59.260 --> 02:07:02.820
Click the playlist on the left for more of
my Scream franchise analysis videos,

02:07:02.820 --> 02:07:04.719
and if you want to see everything you might
have missed in the

02:07:04.719 --> 02:07:08.110
upcoming Scream 7, then make sure you subscribe
to CZsWorld for new

02:07:08.110 --> 02:07:09.260
horrors every week.

02:07:09.260 --> 02:07:13.559
Ring the deathbell for all notifications,
and I will see you in the next one,

02:07:13.559 --> 02:07:17.219
assuming we both survive.

